{"verdicts": [{"id": "F1", "verdict": "REAL", "severity": "minor", "criterion": "needs an unusual input the request doesn't ask to handle, or the cost is cosmetic or diagnostic only", "origin": "introduced", "test_only": false, "failure_scenario": "If the owner's private-strings file can't be read (for example it contains invalid UTF-8) during an implement round eligible for a worker, preparing the worker job throws an ordinary error. The factory then counts it as a task error against the model provider, which resets a degraded provider's failure count and circuit to healthy. The implement stage is marked succeeded with \"error ... no changes\" and no job or session runs, and the run fails later instead of stopping as needs-human at the step that broke.", "reproduction": {"command": "bun test --timeout 120000 $TMPDIR/adj747/f1.test.ts  (pipeline-lan-agent fixture; executor wrapper writes bytes 66 ff fe 0a to <configDir>/private-strings.txt, then delegates to lanAgentExecutor; spies on f.tracker.record)", "output": "F1 threw: PrivateError Cannot read private-strings.txt; publication blocked\nF1 status: failed error: Cannot read private-strings.txt; publication blocked\nF1 jobs: 0 locals: 0\nF1 record calls: [[\"alpha\",\"ok\"],[\"alpha\",\"error\"]]\nF1 implement invocations: [[\"error\",\"Cannot read private-strings.txt; publication blocked\"]]\nF1 implement stage: [[\"succeeded\",\"alpha/m: error: Cannot read private-strings.txt; publication blocked; no changes\"]]"}, "evidence": "lan-agent.ts:32 `const prepared = await publication.prepare();` has no catch, and prepare() in engine.ts:1166 calls `privateStringsDigest(privateEntries(ctx, cwd))`, which can throw PrivateError (loadPrivateStrings in src/gates/private.ts:138). In context.ts invoke's catch only NeedsHumanError sets `needsHuman`. Any other error becomes `status: \"error\"` and reaches `health?.record(target.provider, result.status, …)`, and providers.ts resets `consecutiveFailures = 0; circuitOpenUntil = null` for \"error\". The request says: \"Worker infrastructure failures never reach health. The executor either returns local()'s real result or throws NeedsHumanError\". The same gap applies to other non-NeedsHuman throws in prepare (headSha, git status, ctx.save).", "location": {"file": "src/pipeline/lan-agent.ts", "lines": [32, 33]}, "duplicate_of": null, "fix_status": "yes", "reason": "The later commit wraps publication.prepare() and rethrows any error that is not NeedsHumanError, SimulatedTermination or an abort as NeedsHumanError(\"Cannot prepare worker job: <redacted>\"), so health is not touched."}, {"id": "F2", "verdict": "REAL", "severity": "minor", "criterion": "needs an unusual input the request doesn't ask to handle, or the cost is cosmetic or diagnostic only", "origin": "introduced", "test_only": false, "failure_scenario": "A user cancels the run while the coordinator is waiting on the commit adoption for a worker result that failed confinement, or on the remote-branch read after a failed job. The executor still starts a local agent session with the already-cancelled signal. That session's process is spawned and killed at once, and the run ends cancelled anyway, so the cost is a wasted, briefly started agent process.", "reproduction": {"command": "bun test $TMPDIR/adj747/f2.test.ts  (lan-agent.test.ts fixture; adopt() or remoteSha() held on a deferred promise, controller.abort() called, then released; records whether local() ran and whether the signal was already aborted at that point)", "output": "F2a localCalled true signalAbortedAtLocal true status cancelled\nF2b localCalled true signalAbortedAtLocal true status cancelled"}, "evidence": "lan-agent.ts checks `spec.signal.aborted` only at the top of the loop. After `await publication.adopt(sha, request);` (line 114) the confinement/cancelled branch does `return local();` (line 117), and after `const remote = await publication.remoteSha();` (line 124) it does `return local();` (line 130), both without re-checking the signal. The request treats a worker `status: \"cancelled\"` as an infrastructure failure only \"while the run isn't aborted\". runProcess (proc.ts:993) terminates a child spawned with a pre-aborted signal immediately, which limits the impact.", "location": {"file": "src/pipeline/lan-agent.ts", "lines": [114, 130]}, "duplicate_of": null, "fix_status": "yes", "reason": "The later commit adds `if (spec.signal.aborted) return cancelled(id);` after both adopt() and remoteSha(), and routes the remaining local fallbacks through `fallback()`, which returns cancelled when the signal is aborted."}]}
 aborted, so the final outcome is right and only the local start is wasted.", "location": {"file": "src/pipeline/lan-agent.ts", "lines": [114, 131]}, "duplicate_of": null, "fix_status": "yes", "reason": "Reproduced at head: local() runs once with an aborted signal on both paths; 397e8b47 re-checks spec.signal.aborted after adopt() and remoteSha(), returns cancelled, and routes fallbacks through a cancel-aware helper."}]}
